════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  2-Body Earth-Moon EKF (N-body propagation)
  Observer: lat= 40.0000 lon=  0.0000
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  State vector: x = [e, i, Omega, omega, M0, mu, a]
    e     = eccentricity of Moon orbit
    i     = inclination of Moon orbit to equator (deg)
    Omega = longitude of ascending node (deg)
    omega = argument of periapsis (deg)
    M0    = mean anomaly at epoch (deg)
    mu    = GM_earth + GM_moon (km^3/s^2)
    a     = semi-major axis of Moon orbit (km)

  Key: Moon parallax from Earth surface is ~57 arcmin.
  This directly constrains the distance a, breaking
  the mu-a degeneracy that exists for the distant Sun.
  Loaded   3017 Moon observations
  Round-trip error:  7.141E-10 km

